---
const { osuYears, michYears, seasonProfiles, provenance, matchupMethod, simulationRunCount } = Astro.props;
---
<section class="lab-shell" data-lab data-season-profiles={JSON.stringify(seasonProfiles)}>
  <header class="lab-header"><div><h1>RIVALRY LAB</h1><span>MODEL CARMEN-19.03</span></div><a class="lab-method-link" href="/rivalry-lab/about">METHOD &amp; SOURCES →</a></header>
  <nav class="lab-nav" aria-label="Rivalry Lab steps"><button data-screen="matchup" aria-current="step">1 · Matchup</button><button data-screen="tape">2 · Tape</button><button data-screen="pregame">3 · Pregame</button><button data-screen="game">4 · Game</button></nav>
  <section class="lab-screen" data-view="matchup"><h2><span class="osu">OHIO STATE <b data-osu-year>{osuYears[0]}</b></span> AGAINST <span class="mich">MICHIGAN <b data-mich-year>{michYears[0]}</b></span>, ON NEUTRAL GROUND.</h2><p class="lede">Pick any available Ohio State or Michigan season. Both are translated into one neutral scoring era, then the game is simulated.</p><p class="matchup-coverage">Seasons from 2004 forward use imported game data (possessions, turnovers, efficiency, red zone) when both teams have coverage.</p><div class="selector-box"><label><b class="osu">OHIO STATE</b><select data-osu>{osuYears.map((year: number) => <option value={year} selected={year === osuYears[0]}>{year}</option>)}</select><small data-osu-facts>Loading season profile...</small></label><label><b class="mich">MICHIGAN</b><select data-mich>{michYears.map((year: number) => <option value={year} selected={year === michYears[0]}>{year}</option>)}</select><small data-mich-facts>Loading season profile...</small></label></div><div class="lab-actions"><span>ERA NEUTRAL: each season is translated into a common scoring environment.</span><button class="primary" data-build>BUILD MATCHUP →</button></div></section>
  <section class="lab-screen" data-view="tape" hidden><div class="section-title"><h2>TALE OF THE TAPE</h2><span data-context></span></div><section class="season-profiles" aria-label="Selected season profiles" data-profiles></section><div class="lab-actions"><button class="secondary" data-screen="matchup">← SEASON SELECT</button><button class="primary" data-pregame>SIMULATE MATCHUP →</button></div></section>
  <section class="lab-screen" data-view="pregame" hidden><div class="section-title"><h2>PREGAME</h2><span data-pregame-context></span></div><p class="pregame-lede">Four steps build this forecast. Each one stands on the last, and the simulation runs on the result.</p><section class="step"><header><b>STEP 1</b><h3>GRADE BOTH SEASONS</h3><em>DERIVED</em></header><p>Every team is graded against the average team of its own year: 0 is average, higher is better. Grading inside each year lets any two eras meet on even ground.</p><div class="step-inputs" data-input-list></div></section><section class="step"><header><b>STEP 2</b><h3>TURN THE GAPS INTO POINTS</h3><em>DERIVED</em></header><p>Each offense is matched against the other defense, the overall gap is added, and the result becomes points.</p><div class="driver-grid"><article><b class="osu">OHIO STATE</b><p data-osu-driver></p></article><article><b class="mich">MICHIGAN</b><p data-mich-driver></p></article></div></section><section class="step"><header><b>STEP 3</b><h3>SET THE EXPECTED SCORE</h3><em>DERIVED</em></header><p>An average team scores about 25 points. Each side starts at 25 and moves by its Step 2 points.</p><div class="step-score" data-expected-score><strong class="score" data-score>--</strong><span class="step-margin" data-expected-margin><b data-margin>--</b><small>Ohio State minus Michigan</small></span></div></section><section class="step"><header><b>STEP 4</b><h3>TURN THE MARGIN INTO A CHANCE</h3><em>DERIVED</em></header><p>The bigger the expected margin, the more often that side wins. This is each team's chance of winning before a single simulated snap.</p><div class="step-probability" data-win-probability><div class="probability"><div><strong class="osu" data-osu-prob>--%</strong><b>OHIO STATE</b></div><div><strong class="mich" data-mich-prob>--%</strong><b>MICHIGAN</b></div></div><div class="prob-bar"><i data-osu-bar></i><i data-mich-bar></i></div></div></section><section class="pregame-play" data-pregame-play><p>Pick this matchup, then simulate it. The model plays {simulationRunCount.toLocaleString('en-US')} repeated games of the same matchup and reports the results, plus one of those games drive by drive. Every run draws its own games.</p><button class="primary play-one" data-run="1">SIMULATE</button></section><section class="provenance" data-testid="snapshot-provenance"><b>SOURCES &amp; PROVENANCE</b><p>Derived ratings: public Rivalry Lab product snapshot, generated {new Date(provenance.generatedAt).toISOString().slice(0, 10)}.</p><p>Snapshot: {provenance.ratingModelVersion} ratings · {provenance.eraModelVersion} era translation · {provenance.dataSnapshotVersion} data coverage.</p><p><a href="/rivalry-lab/about">READ THE METHOD</a></p></section></section>
  <section class="lab-screen" data-view="game" hidden><div class="game-score" data-game-score></div><section class="model-call" data-model-call hidden aria-label="The model's results"><div class="section-title"><h3>THE MODEL'S RESULTS</h3><span>SIMULATED</span></div><p class="call-note" data-call-note></p><p class="call-headline" data-call-favorite></p><p class="call-share" data-call-share></p><p class="call-one-score" data-call-one-score></p><p class="call-upset" data-call-upset></p><div class="call-extremes" data-call-extremes></div><details class="breakdown" data-breakdown><summary>SEE THE FULL BREAKDOWN</summary><div class="breakdown-body"><div class="breakdown-wins" data-breakdown-wins></div><div class="margin-chart" data-margin-chart aria-label="Final margin distribution"></div><div class="breakdown-facts" data-breakdown-facts></div><p class="breakdown-provenance" data-breakdown-versions></p></div></details></section><p class="run-game-label" data-run-game-label hidden></p><section class="timeline" aria-label="Simulated drive timeline" data-timeline></section><div class="game-grid"><article data-game-stats></article></div></section>
  <footer>Rivalry Lab uses historical season data. Simulated games are model-generated, not historical results. Not affiliated with either university.</footer>
</section>
<script>
   type TeamId = 'ohio-state' | 'michigan';
   type SeasonProfile = { observed: { conference: string | null; division: string | null; coach: string | null; finalApRank: number | null; cfbdPostseasonRank: number | null; pointsPerGame: number | null; pointsAllowedPerGame: number | null }; derived: { overallRank: number | null; offenseRank: number | null; defenseRank: number | null; scheduleStrengthRank: number | null; ratedTeams: number | null }; confidence: { score: number | null; reasons: string[] } };
     type ProfileEntry = { teamId: TeamId; season: number; wins: number; losses: number; ties: number; crossEra: { overall: number; offense: number; defense: number }; profile: SeasonProfile | null };
    type MatchupResponse = { matchup: { neutralPointsPerTeam: number; ohioState: { expectedScore: number; winProbability: number; scoreAdvantage: number }; michigan: { expectedScore: number; winProbability: number; scoreAdvantage: number }; expectedMargin: number } };
   const root = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-lab]')!; const select = <T extends HTMLElement>(selector: string) => root.querySelector<T>(selector)!;
   const profiles = JSON.parse(root.dataset.seasonProfiles ?? '[]') as ProfileEntry[];
   let matchup: MatchupResponse['matchup'];
   const generateSeed = () => String(Math.floor(10_000_000 + Math.random() * 90_000_000));
   let roundSeed = generateSeed(); let runIndex = 0;
   const state = () => ({ osuYear: Number(select<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-osu]').value), michYear: Number(select<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-mich]').value) });
   const track = (event: string, properties: Record<string, string | number>) => (window as Window & { gtag?: (...args: unknown[]) => void }).gtag?.('event', event, properties);
    async function getMatchup() { const { osuYear, michYear } = state(); const response = await fetch(`/api/matchup?osuYear=${osuYear}&michYear=${michYear}`); const payload = await response.json(); if (!response.ok) throw new Error(payload.error); matchup = payload.matchup; select('[data-osu-year]').textContent = String(osuYear); select('[data-mich-year]').textContent = String(michYear); const selectorSummary=(teamId:TeamId,year:number)=>{const entry=profiles.find((item)=>item.teamId===teamId&&item.season===year);if(!entry)return 'Profile not available in current source coverage.';const ap=entry.profile?.observed.finalApRank;const coach=entry.profile?.observed.coach??'Coach not available in current source coverage.';return `${entry.wins}-${entry.losses}${entry.ties?`-${entry.ties}`:''} · ${ap===null||ap===undefined?'Final AP rank not available in current source coverage.':`Final AP #${ap}`} · ${coach}`}; select('[data-osu-facts]').textContent=selectorSummary('ohio-state',osuYear); select('[data-mich-facts]').textContent=selectorSummary('michigan',michYear); const context = `${osuYear} OHIO STATE × ${michYear} MICHIGAN · ERA NEUTRAL`; select('[data-context]').textContent = context; select('[data-pregame-context]').textContent = context; renderTape(); renderPregame(); }
  function show(screen: string) { if (screen === 'tape') { roundSeed = generateSeed(); runIndex = 0; } root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-view]').forEach((view) => view.hidden = view.dataset.view !== screen); root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('.lab-nav button').forEach((button) => button.setAttribute('aria-current', button.dataset.screen === screen ? 'step' : 'false')); }
  const percentage = (value: number) => `${Math.round(value * 100)}%`;
   function rankLabel(rank: number | null, ratedTeams: number | null) { return rank === null ? 'UNRANKED' : `NO. ${rank}${ratedTeams === null ? '' : ` OF ${ratedTeams}`}`; }
   function profileCard(teamId: TeamId, season: number, teamName: string, color: string) { const profile = profiles.find((entry) => entry.teamId === teamId && entry.season === season)?.profile; if (!profile) return `<article class="season-profile ${color}" data-testid="season-profile-${teamId}"><header><b>${teamName} · ${season}</b><em>PROFILE UNAVAILABLE</em></header><p>This public snapshot has no observed or derived profile for this season.</p></article>`; const { observed, derived, confidence } = profile; const conference = [observed.conference, observed.division].filter(Boolean).join(' · ') || 'Conference not reported'; return `<article class="season-profile ${color}" data-testid="season-profile-${teamId}"><header><b>${teamName} · ${season}</b><em>SEASON PROFILE</em></header><p class="profile-record">${conference} · ${observed.coach ?? 'Coach not reported'}</p><div class="profile-facts"><span><small>OBSERVED SCORING</small><strong>${observed.pointsPerGame === null ? 'NOT REPORTED' : `${observed.pointsPerGame.toFixed(1)} PPG`}</strong><i>${observed.pointsAllowedPerGame === null ? 'Points allowed not reported' : `${observed.pointsAllowedPerGame.toFixed(1)} allowed per game`}</i></span><span><small>OBSERVED FINAL AP</small><strong>${observed.finalApRank === null ? 'UNRANKED' : `NO. ${observed.finalApRank}`}</strong><i>${observed.cfbdPostseasonRank === null ? 'CFBD postseason rank unavailable' : `CFBD postseason: No. ${observed.cfbdPostseasonRank}`}</i></span></div><div class="profile-ranks"><small>DERIVED SRS RANKINGS</small><span>OVERALL <b>${rankLabel(derived.overallRank, derived.ratedTeams)}</b></span><span>OFFENSE <b>${rankLabel(derived.offenseRank, derived.ratedTeams)}</b></span><span>DEFENSE <b>${rankLabel(derived.defenseRank, derived.ratedTeams)}</b></span><span>SCHEDULE <b>${rankLabel(derived.scheduleStrengthRank, derived.ratedTeams)}</b></span></div><p class="profile-confidence"><b>SNAPSHOT CONFIDENCE ${confidence.score === null ? 'NOT SCORED' : `${confidence.score}%`}</b>${confidence.reasons.length ? ` · ${confidence.reasons[0]}` : ''}</p></article>`; }
    function renderProfiles() { const { osuYear, michYear } = state(); select('[data-profiles]').innerHTML = `<div class="profile-grid">${profileCard('ohio-state', osuYear, 'OHIO STATE', 'osu')}${profileCard('michigan', michYear, 'MICHIGAN', 'mich')}</div>`; }
    function renderTape() { renderProfiles(); }
   function renderPregame() { const { osuYear, michYear } = state(); const osu = profiles.find((entry) => entry.teamId === 'ohio-state' && entry.season === osuYear)!; const mich = profiles.find((entry) => entry.teamId === 'michigan' && entry.season === michYear)!; select('[data-osu-prob]').textContent = percentage(matchup.ohioState.winProbability); select('[data-mich-prob]').textContent = percentage(matchup.michigan.winProbability); (select<HTMLElement>('[data-osu-bar]')).style.width = percentage(matchup.ohioState.winProbability); (select<HTMLElement>('[data-mich-bar]')).style.width = percentage(matchup.michigan.winProbability); select('[data-score]').innerHTML = `<span class="mich">${Math.round(matchup.michigan.expectedScore)} MICH</span> – <span class="osu">${Math.round(matchup.ohioState.expectedScore)} OSU</span>`; select('[data-margin]').textContent = `${matchup.expectedMargin >= 0 ? '+' : ''}${matchup.expectedMargin.toFixed(1)} OSU`; const driverText = (team: string, advantage: number) => `The model expects ${team} to score ${Math.abs(advantage).toFixed(1)} points ${advantage >= 0 ? 'more' : 'fewer'} than an average team.`; select('[data-osu-driver]').textContent = driverText('Ohio State', matchup.ohioState.scoreAdvantage); select('[data-mich-driver]').textContent = driverText('Michigan', matchup.michigan.scoreAdvantage); select('[data-input-list]').innerHTML = [['Ohio State offense rating', osu.crossEra.offense, 'osu'], ['Ohio State defense rating', osu.crossEra.defense, 'osu'], ['Ohio State overall rating', osu.crossEra.overall, 'osu'], ['Michigan offense rating', mich.crossEra.offense, 'mich'], ['Michigan defense rating', mich.crossEra.defense, 'mich'], ['Michigan overall rating', mich.crossEra.overall, 'mich']].map(([label, value, color]) => `<span><small>${String(label).toUpperCase()}</small><strong class="${color}">${Number(value).toFixed(3)}</strong></span>`).join(''); }
    async function simulate() { const seed = `${roundSeed}-${runIndex}`; const response = await fetch('/api/simulate', { method: 'POST', headers: { 'content-type': 'application/json' }, body: JSON.stringify({ ...state(), seed }) }); const payload = await response.json(); if (!response.ok) throw new Error(payload.error); runIndex += 1; const { osuYear, michYear } = state(); track('rivalry_lab_simulation_run', { osu_season: osuYear, michigan_season: michYear, simulation_count: payload.series.runCount }); renderGame(payload); renderModelCall(payload); show('game'); }
   function renderGame(payload: any) { const game = payload.result; const series = payload.series; select('[data-game-score]').innerHTML = `<div><b class="mich">MICHIGAN</b><strong>${series.michigan.typicalScore}</strong></div><span>TYPICAL SCORE<br><small>${series.runCount.toLocaleString('en-US')} GAMES</small></span><div><b class="osu">OHIO STATE</b><strong>${series.ohioState.typicalScore}</strong></div>`; const runGameLabel = select('[data-run-game-label]'); runGameLabel.hidden = false; runGameLabel.textContent = `ONE GAME FROM THE RUN · MICHIGAN ${game.michigan.points}, OHIO STATE ${game.ohioState.points}${game.overtime ? ' (OT)' : ''}${payload.representative?.matchesTypicalScore ? '' : ' · CLOSEST GAME TO THE TYPICAL SCORE'}`; let lastQuarter = 0; select('[data-timeline]').innerHTML = game.drives.map((drive: any, index: number) => { const marker = drive.quarter !== lastQuarter ? `<b class="q-mark">${drive.quarter === 5 ? 'OT' : `Q${drive.quarter}`}</b>` : ''; lastQuarter = drive.quarter; return `${marker}<i title="${drive.quarter === 5 ? 'OT' : `Q${drive.quarter}`} · ${drive.outcome}" class="${drive.teamId === 'michigan' ? 'mich-bg' : 'osu-bg'}" style="animation-delay:${index * 40}ms">${drive.outcome}</i>`; }).join(''); select('[data-game-stats]').innerHTML = `<b>TEAM STATS · THIS GAME</b><p><span>Ohio State</span> ${game.ohioState.possessions} possessions · ${game.ohioState.turnovers} turnovers</p><p><span>Michigan</span> ${game.michigan.possessions} possessions · ${game.michigan.turnovers} turnovers</p>`; }
   // Caption rule: every model-call and breakdown sentence reports simulated results only
   // (teams, counts, rates, scores, margins). No tactics, game plans, player traits,
   // coaching decisions, or conditions-for-victory phrasing ("needs to", "the key is",
   // "if they can", "because", "thanks to").
   const TEAM_NAMES: Record<string, string> = { 'ohio-state': 'Ohio State', michigan: 'Michigan' };
   function renderModelCall(payload: any) { const series = payload.series; const favoriteName = TEAM_NAMES[series.favorite]; const underdogId = series.favorite === 'ohio-state' ? 'michigan' : 'ohio-state'; const underdogName = TEAM_NAMES[underdogId]; const sideOf = (teamId: string) => teamId === 'ohio-state' ? series.ohioState : series.michigan; const rate = (value: number) => `${Math.round(value * 100)}%`; const call = select('[data-model-call]'); call.hidden = false; const upset = series.underdogWinRate > 0.5; const leaderId = series.ohioState.wins >= series.michigan.wins ? 'ohio-state' : 'michigan'; select('[data-call-note]').textContent = `The model played this matchup ${series.runCount.toLocaleString('en-US')} times. Every number here comes from that run.`; select('[data-call-favorite]').textContent = upset ? `UPSET: ${underdogName.toUpperCase()} WON MOST GAMES` : `${favoriteName.toUpperCase()} WAS FAVORED`; select('[data-call-share]').textContent = `${TEAM_NAMES[leaderId]} won ${rate(sideOf(leaderId).winRate)} of them.`; select('[data-call-one-score]').textContent = `${rate(series.oneScore.rate)} OF GAMES ENDED WITHIN ONE SCORE (8 POINTS OR FEWER)`; const underdogPregame = Math.round((underdogId === 'ohio-state' ? payload.matchup.ohioState.winProbability : payload.matchup.michigan.winProbability) * 100); const underdogSimulated = Math.round(series.underdogWinRate * 100); const pregameDelta = underdogSimulated - underdogPregame; select('[data-call-upset]').textContent = `UNDERDOG CHECK · PREGAME GAVE ${underdogName.toUpperCase()} ${underdogPregame}%; THE RUN DELIVERED ${underdogSimulated}% (${pregameDelta >= 0 ? '+' : ''}${pregameDelta} PTS)`; const biggestWinTile = (label: string, win: { margin: number; ohioState: number; michigan: number } | null, color: string) => { if (win === null) return `<span><small>${label}</small><strong>NONE IN THIS RUN</strong></span>`; const winnerFirst = color === 'osu' ? `${win.ohioState}–${win.michigan}` : `${win.michigan}–${win.ohioState}`; return `<span><small>${label}</small><strong class="${color}">${winnerFirst}</strong><i>won by ${win.margin}</i></span>`; }; select('[data-call-extremes]').innerHTML = biggestWinTile('BIGGEST OHIO STATE WIN', series.biggestWin.ohioState, 'osu') + biggestWinTile('BIGGEST MICHIGAN WIN', series.biggestWin.michigan, 'mich'); select('[data-breakdown-wins]').innerHTML = `<span><small>OHIO STATE WINS</small><strong class="osu">${series.ohioState.wins.toLocaleString()}</strong><i>${rate(series.ohioState.winRate)} of ${series.runCount.toLocaleString()} games</i></span><span><small>MICHIGAN WINS</small><strong class="mich">${series.michigan.wins.toLocaleString()}</strong><i>${rate(series.michigan.winRate)} of ${series.runCount.toLocaleString()} games</i></span>`; const maxBucket = Math.max(...series.marginBuckets.map((bucket: any) => bucket.games), 1); select('[data-margin-chart]').innerHTML = `<small>FINAL MARGIN · ${series.runCount.toLocaleString()} GAMES</small>` + series.marginBuckets.map((bucket: any) => `<div class="margin-row"><small>${bucket.label}</small><div class="margin-bar"><i class="${bucket.label.startsWith('MICHIGAN') ? 'mich-bg' : 'osu-bg'}" style="width:${(bucket.games / maxBucket) * 100}%"></i></div><b>${bucket.games.toLocaleString()}</b></div>`).join(''); select('[data-breakdown-facts]').innerHTML = [['OVERTIME RATE', rate(series.overtime.rate)], ['ONE-SCORE GAMES (8 OR FEWER)', rate(series.oneScore.rate)], ['BLOWOUTS (17 OR MORE)', rate(series.blowout.rate)], ['OHIO STATE TURNOVERS PER GAME', series.ohioState.averageTurnovers.toFixed(1)], ['MICHIGAN TURNOVERS PER GAME', series.michigan.averageTurnovers.toFixed(1)], [`${underdogName.toUpperCase()} PREGAME WIN PROBABILITY`, `${underdogPregame}%`], [`${underdogName.toUpperCase()} WIN RATE IN THE RUN`, `${underdogSimulated}%`], ['DATA COVERAGE', payload.simulationCoverage === 'rich-game-data' ? 'RICH DATA' : 'SCORE-SCHEDULE']].map(([label, value]) => `<span><small>${label}</small><strong>${value}</strong></span>`).join(''); select('[data-breakdown-versions]').textContent = `Model ${payload.versions.simulationEngineVersion} · ${payload.versions.ratingModelVersion} ratings · ${payload.versions.eraModelVersion} era translation · ${payload.versions.adjustmentModelVersion} opponent adjustment · ${payload.versions.dataSnapshotVersion} data.`; }
    root.addEventListener('click', async (event) => { const target = (event.target as HTMLElement).closest<HTMLButtonElement>('button'); if (!target) return; try { if (target.dataset.screen) show(target.dataset.screen); if (target.matches('[data-build]')) { await getMatchup(); const { osuYear, michYear } = state(); track('rivalry_lab_matchup_built', { osu_season: osuYear, michigan_season: michYear, era_mode: 'neutral' }); show('tape'); } if (target.matches('[data-pregame]')) { await getMatchup(); show('pregame'); } if (target.matches('[data-run="1"]')) await simulate(); } catch (error) { alert(error instanceof Error ? error.message : 'Unable to run Rivalry Lab'); } });
   select('[data-osu]').addEventListener('change', () => void getMatchup()); select('[data-mich]').addEventListener('change', () => void getMatchup());
  void getMatchup();
</script>


<script>
  const coverageLab = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-lab]');
  const coveragePregame = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-view="pregame"]');

  async function renderSimulationCoverage() {
    if (!coverageLab || !coveragePregame) return;
    const osuYear = coverageLab.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-osu]')?.value;
    const michYear = coverageLab.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-mich]')?.value;
    if (!osuYear || !michYear) return;
    const response = await fetch(`/api/matchup?osuYear=${osuYear}&michYear=${michYear}`);
    if (!response.ok) return;
    const { simulationCoverage } = await response.json() as { simulationCoverage: 'rich-game-data' | 'score-and-schedule' };
    const coverageLabel = simulationCoverage === 'rich-game-data' ? 'RICH DATA' : 'SCORE-SCHEDULE';
    const coverage = simulationCoverage === 'rich-game-data'
      ? 'Imported game data is active: both selected seasons carry possession, turnover, efficiency, and red-zone inputs.'
      : 'Score and schedule context is active. Imported game data stays off unless both selected seasons have rich coverage.';
    let pregameContext = coveragePregame.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-simulation-coverage]');
    if (!pregameContext) {
      pregameContext = document.createElement('aside');
      pregameContext.dataset.simulationCoverage = '';
      pregameContext.className = 'simulation-coverage';
      coveragePregame.querySelector('[data-pregame-play]')?.before(pregameContext);
    }
    pregameContext.innerHTML = `<b>SIMULATION COVERAGE · ${coverageLabel}</b><p>${coverage}</p>`;
  }

  new MutationObserver(() => {
    if (coveragePregame && !coveragePregame.hidden) void renderSimulationCoverage();
  }).observe(coverageLab!, { attributes: true, subtree: true, attributeFilter: ['hidden'] });
  coverageLab?.querySelectorAll('select').forEach((input) => input.addEventListener('change', () => void renderSimulationCoverage()));
</script>

<script>
  const lab = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-lab]');
  let restoringHistory = false;
  const applyScreen = (screen: string) => {
    lab?.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-view]').forEach((view) => {
      view.hidden = view.dataset.view !== screen;
    });
  };
  // A fresh page load always starts at season select: the later screens hold state that
  // lives only in this browser session, so restoring them from the hash lands on empty
  // shells. Back and forward still walk the screens visited since this load.
  history.replaceState({ screen: 'matchup' }, '', '#matchup');
  window.addEventListener('popstate', () => {
    const screen = window.location.hash.slice(1) || 'matchup';
    restoringHistory = true;
    applyScreen(screen);
    window.setTimeout(() => { restoringHistory = false; }, 0);
  });
  new MutationObserver(() => {
    if (restoringHistory || !lab) return;
    const screen = lab.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-view]:not([hidden])')?.dataset.view;
    if (screen && window.location.hash !== `#${screen}`) history.pushState({ screen }, '', `#${screen}`);
  }).observe(lab!, { attributes: true, subtree: true, attributeFilter: ['hidden'] });
</script>


<style is:global>
    .lab-header { display:flex;align-items:end;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px; }.lab-method-link,.lab-nav a { color:#111;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:700;text-decoration:underline 3px #bb0000;text-underline-offset:6px;white-space:nowrap; }.lab-nav a { padding:0 0 4px; }
